WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:03.800
Man, we've been on a roll recently.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.740
How do you still have so much
energy after all the walking we've done?

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.340
Miyazumi. May I have a word?

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.460
Hey, Usuyama, what's up?

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.580
[Usuyama Toru, 29, SB Quality Assurance]
You agreed to a package deal with Waoko
without consulting me again.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:20.300
Package deal?

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:25.440
You know, free stuff. Like getting
free detergent when buying a 4-pack of beer.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.240
Oh, right, I guess you haven't met yet.
This is our newbie…

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.420
Oh, I know him.
He's on the team, isn't he?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:37.820
This is Usuyama from QA.
He used to play badminton too, you know?

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:39.820
I'm still trying to get him to join the team.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.960
How about we talk about that package deal?

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:44.240
How about you let Sales do our job…

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.540
You're quickly approaching the limit set by
the Act against Unjustifiable Premiums.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:52.440
Oh, please. I've been doing this for years.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.440
And that's what makes you careless!

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:59.080
One way or another,
I want to see that paperwork in QA.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.300
Fine, jeez.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.660
So… what's the scary guy's deal?

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.740
QA is full of serious guys,
but he's downright pedantic.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.440
So… what's QA anyway?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.660
Quality Assurance Department.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.360
They're basically our very own corporate cops.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:25.740
Making sure the labels are accurate,
that ingredients meet industry standards.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:29.480
They keep an eye on us to assure
we follow the law and company policy.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:30.880
Keep an eye…

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:36.420
But it's thanks to QA that our customers
get to safely enjoy our products.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.280
They're a pain in the ass,
but we need them.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.920
We're back!

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:44.620
Congratulations, Shiratori!

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:46.900
They chose your idea!

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:48.000
[1. Scallion Ginger Ale]
[2. Orange Juice (Red)]

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:51.520
Mine…?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.460
[#03: Brainstorming]

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:32.540
Never thought getting time off work
could be this easy. All thanks to you, Mikoto!

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:33.840
This ain't a field trip.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:37.920
We'll get a tour of the Tatebayashi factory
and help Shiratori with his proposal.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:39.500
Sounds like work to me.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:41.480
[Badminton Team Get-Together]
Yeah, really screams "work."

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:42.980
We know what we're here for.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.840
I'm surprised we all get to go.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:49.280
We've definitely got Tatsu to thank for that.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.780
I'm guessing that means
he just begged the president.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:53.980
Sure did!

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.580
Our president has a
huge soft spot for Tatsu.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.260
How did I even end up here…?

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.200
Come on, man, you get to be the star today!

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:13.120
You've got a whole team of the highest
quality colleagues to help your sorry ass.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.120
I don't recall asking for help.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.360
We should've held a badminton
training camp, not this.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:23.580
Shiratori. You're not a kid anymore.
It's time to stop acting like one.

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:28.100
If you keep sucking at your job,
they'll take you off the team.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:32.140
Yeah, not happening.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:36.380
All you need to do is get
the project proposal out of the way.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.140
Yup!

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:40.160
The Badrymen've got your back!

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.280
Okay, fine.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.280
So… what's a project proposal anyway?

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:55.120
Does Shiratori even know how to
write a project proposal?

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.400
Toya from the Planning Department
went with him, he should be fine.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.120
Lucky him. Wish I could've
also gone on the tour.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.340
No, Yata, you just want to skip work.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.660
How'd you guess?

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.260
I know you don't care about factory tours!

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:11.760
Executive director!

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.360
Good morning, sir!

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.260
Good to know the Badminton
team is having fun.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:19.740
[On-site training: Miyazumi, Takeda, Shiratori]
Good to know the Badminton
team is having fun.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:29.520
The market has really expanded
over the past few years,

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:34.320
so the Tatebayashi factory will install new
equipment this summer to increase production.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:39.240
Thanks to the Sales Department,
Besshonuma Cider really took off last year,

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.700
causing us to temporarily
expand the production line.

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:46.220
I'm quite a fan of that product myself.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.780
Yes, my daughter drinks it all the time too!

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.940
It appeals to a broad demographic!

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.740
This place ain't half bad!

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.080
You really know your stuff, Tatsu!

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:05.420
Heck yeah, I do. Alright, leave your stuff in your
rooms, and let's head to the conference room.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:09.640
[New Product Idea
(Scallion Ginger Ale) Discussion]
Alright, time for that project proposal.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.880
Do I have to write it myself?

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.060
It was your idea, after all.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:20.340
Think about doubles: we can't have
a proper game if we don't fulfill our roles.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:25.500
Right now, your role is
writing a project proposal.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:27.640
What's he on about?

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:30.160
He wanted to shoehorn in
a badminton reference.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:31.660
[Product name: Scallion Ginger Ale]

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.320
But this is…

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:34.720
This one's really out there.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.040
At least it's better than Natto Cola?

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.460
What do you mean, "at least"?
Natto Cola is great.

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:42.760
Honestly, I don't even know
why they went ahead with this.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.920
Why scallions anyway?

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:49.920
Recently at the diner, I had some Fukaya scallions
and ginger ale and thought it was a good mix…

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:54.940
Suppose that's as good a reason as any.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:58.660
Well, let's get started, then…

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.780
[Scallion Ginger Ale Project Proposal]

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:04.760
The thing is, I don't even know
how to write a project proposal…

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:09.460
That's fine. We can start by brainstorming
this Scallion Ginger Ale of yours.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:16.300
Let's figure out the selling point,
or where you'd like to sell it.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.180
All that goes into the project proposal.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.680
Glad we have an expert on board!

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:21.740
Sounds good to me.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:25.580
Wanna do a SWOT analysis?

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:28.760
They're usually used for management strategies,

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:34.300
but since we're already teaching
Shiratori new skills, might as well.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:35.880
You've got a point.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:42.560
Oh, good call! If we can iron out the details,
that should give Mikoto some ideas!

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:45.620
SWOT stands for…

00:07:45.720 --> 00:07:46.440
Strengths

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:47.300
Weaknesses,

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.240
Opportunities,

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.280
and Threats.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:50.740
Straightforward, right?

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:57.380
Once we figure out all of these,
we'll know what to do with Scallion Ginger Ale.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:02.380
A strength of Scallion Ginger Ale…?

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:04.880
It stands out, if nothing else.

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:09.200
But the flavor profile is so niche,
most normal people won't buy it.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.460
That's the thing. What do you think?

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:17.080
What, um… like, it might
go well with a meal?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:21.360
People do drink ginger ale with meals,
so that might work for us too.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.660
Fukaya scallions are a local specialty,
so it could work as a souvenir!

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:25.940
Sounds healthy!

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:26.920
It sure does!

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.440
Plus, recently…

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.320
We end up with… this.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.760
So what do we do with this?

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:43.220
Now we combine them with
each other and analyze what we get.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.300
First up, strengths and opportunities.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:54.320
Standing out will definitely
make it work as a souvenir.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:59.140
[Drinking Scallion Ginger Ale for the first time!]
If influencers catch on to it,
that should give us some attention.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:02.000
That'd do wonders for our marketing budget!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.560
Making a meal that goes
well with it should work too!

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:07.820
[We made the BEST recipe!]
Cooking livestreams are popular these days -
you might be onto something!

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:11.140
Okay, things aren't as bad as I thought.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.740
So… weaknesses and threats are up next?

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:18.940
Saitama already has plenty of souvenirs…

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:22.700
Like Hyakumangoku buns or Koedo Sour…

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:28.000
Yeah, it needs something special
to stand out from the crowd.

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:30.240
Something that makes you wanna pick it up?

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:33.720
Yeah! Something to attract people's attention.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:40.260
How about… a ramune bottle?

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:45.260
We could… put it in a ramune bottle?

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:48.960
I can see the visual appeal.

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:53.640
It's got a nice color to it,
so that should catch people's eyes.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.060
Feels very retro. I like it.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:59.480
Then we should make
a cute label to go with it!

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:02.580
So cute that people
post aesthetic photos of it online?

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:05.540
That might even distract people from the flavor.

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:08.520
I know! Should we make a mascot to go with it?

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:10.020
Please, anything but a mascot…

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.300
Okay! It's coming together nicely!

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.820
This might actually work!

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:22.260
I gotta admit… you might've hit the bullseye
with that ramune bottle.

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:28.640
Alright. Wanna go ahead
and write all that down?

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:29.580
Yep!

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.040
[Sca]

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:40.560
[Scallion]

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.480
It's like I'm watching my grandpa…

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:48.700
I see now why your daily reports
always came in so late…

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:51.420
Can you stop?! You're distracting me…

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:56.980
If I could just use the flick input​
on my smartphone, I'd be much faster, okay?!

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:58.850
Right, I'll keep myself busy, then.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.280
At this rate, we'll be here until morning…

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.720
Never again…

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:20.180
Wow, this place is huge!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.520
If it's so huge, why do you feel
the need to sit right next to me?

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:32.540
Loosen up, we're way overdue on bonding time.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.760
What makes you think I'd want to "bond"?

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.100
Man, this is divine.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.920
And I here I thought I could finally be alone…

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:46.090
I just want to play badminton.

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:50.020
Why do I have to bother with Sales
and proposals and all that nonsense?

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.760
Because it's your job.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:57.680
For us, work and badminton are
two parts of the same whole.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:03.100
Project proposals, SWOTs,
that's all so out of my league…

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:06.200
And for now, that's all well and good.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:11.960
But let me tell you something that stays true
no matter what you're dealing with.

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:17.060
Things can only go well
if you put your heart into them.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:20.240
That goes for
project proposals, and for doubles.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:25.220
When your heart's in the game,
you'll hit every shot.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:28.680
Your project proposal should get accepted too.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.660
There are some things you can't do,
no matter how hard you try…

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:43.940
I know I asked you after our game with Uni,
but… something happened to you, didn't it?

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:50.140
You're not the type of guy
who'd just ignore his weaknesses, so…

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:57.320
Well, anyway, I'll go
wash my hair or something.

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:02.880
I'm scared…

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.080
…of jumping backwards.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:10.860
Back in high school, during the Interhigh…

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:14.960
I was partnered with this guy…

00:13:24.340 --> 00:13:25.940
You okay, Azuma?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.820
Yeah… Leave the back to me.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.380
You just focus on scoring, alright?

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.640
Tachibana, are you okay?!
Someone get him a stretcher!

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:01.940
He can't play badminton anymore.

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:04.060
All because of me.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:11.560
We'd been partners for so long,
I couldn't wrap my head around it…

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:15.760
So I ran away to Mitsuhoshi…

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:19.620
And I couldn't jump backwards anymore…

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:25.280
It all comes flooding back to me
when I get into that spot…

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:28.060
My body just freezes in place.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:30.240
Wow…

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:33.000
Well, you've got nothing to worry about now.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.460
Because I've got your back.

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:41.960
Who says you need to jump?

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:47.840
I'm stronger than you anyway.

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:50.740
What? Since when?

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:53.000
Since I beat you on your first day here?

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:56.520
D-Don't get so cocky just
because you got lucky one time!

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.740
I'll have you know, it's properly caring
for my body that makes me so strong!

00:15:00.740 --> 00:15:03.680
Does that "care" involve being
passed out drunk on a playground?

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:04.940
That's besides the point!

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:07.720
That felt amazing.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.220
Bit too hot for me.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.120
Happy birthday!

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:17.860
What's all this?

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:22.200
What, did you forget you're turning 20 today?

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:25.540
To celebrate your hard work,
we put together a little surprise.

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:29.580
Come, birthday boy, you're sitting here.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:30.360
Wai…

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.980
Toya! I didn't ask for this!

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:37.240
Don't look at me, this was all Tatsuru's work.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:41.000
Toya just happened to tell
me it was your birthday.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:43.360
Not bad given the short notice, right?

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:46.960
Why do all this for me…?

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:50.740
What do you mean, "why"?
We're buddies now.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:58.280
We're all buddies,
plus you're officially an adult now.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:01.160
Why not toast to that with our
company's very own liquor?

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:03.240
Heck yeah!

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:04.700
Have your pick!

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:14.060
To everyone's hard work today, and
to Shiratori Mikoto for his birthday…

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:16.200
Cheers!

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:20.780
That hits the spot!

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:23.320
Tatsuru, that makes you sound like an old man!

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:25.240
Honestly, kids these days…

00:16:33.820 --> 00:16:35.940
What?! Why is it so bitter?

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.980
Because you've got baby taste buds.

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:40.920
Take it easy, you just turned 20 yourself.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.120
It's been five weeks!

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:46.680
Shiratori Mikoto drinking his first can
of alcohol on his 20h birthday!

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:49.100
So, how's our craft beer?

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:52.080
You can tell it's the good stuff, right?

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:54.700
I really can't.

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:58.400
You're not doing half bad
for your first time.

00:16:58.400 --> 00:16:59.940
Just don't push it, 'kay?

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:00.780
It's so bitter…

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:12.080
Mikoto… I think you've had enough.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:14.320
Don't forget we've still got work tomorrow.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.240
I'm fine!

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.320
Yeah, this is a good place to stop.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:22.240
Hey, give it back!

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:24.900
Here, have some water instead.

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:27.340
Hey!

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:30.160
Seriously, you're gonna hurt yourself!

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.040
This is exactly why…

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.160
This is exactly why
the SB Badminton team sucks!

00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:42.680
Let me SWOT analyze
everything wrong with you!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.720
Takeda, you're first!

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:45.640
Me?!

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.960
Seriously, what's with the stage fright?

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:51.380
Missing the shuttle while serving over and over
just because a few people are watching!

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.000
No…!

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:53.020
This isn't much of a SWOT, is it?
No…!

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:55.340
This isn't much of a SWOT, is it?

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:58.180
The games are public,
obviously there's gonna be an audience!

00:17:58.200 --> 00:17:58.980
Yes, sir!

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.000
Toya!

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:02.420
You rely on your instincts too much!

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:06.080
How about your start using your head
and stop half-assing everything!

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:06.840
Huh?!

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:10.180
You haven't improved
even a bit since high school!

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:12.520
I know you can do better than that!

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:15.000
Stop thinking your reflexes
will save you every time!

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.720
You know he's right, Toya.

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:18.700
Sota, I see you!

00:18:18.920 --> 00:18:21.860
Don't you think you're taking it too easy?

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:28.120
What, do you think pretending
you don't care makes you look cool?

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:31.200
If you're not going to give your best out there…

00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:33.900
…you might as well be running away!

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:35.980
Running away… running away… running away…

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.320
And finally, you!

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:41.920
I didn't know it was possible to waste
so much energy until I met you!

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:44.220
You've been playing badminton for years!

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:47.300
Can't you use your brain and
move more efficiently on the court?!

00:18:47.300 --> 00:18:50.100
Children put more thought
into how they play than you!

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:56.440
That being said…

00:18:56.920 --> 00:19:02.380
I've been told that Takeda's been
covering my ass at work.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:06.600
And you did help me a lot today…

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:08.440
I appreciate it!

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:10.820
Oh, no, it's nothing…

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:15.780
And Toya, I feel like I can always
be honest with you…

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:17.880
So, yeah, I'm grateful!

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:18.780
Sure…

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:20.160
And Sota…

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:22.820
You also helped me today…

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:27.020
Thank you…!

00:19:27.080 --> 00:19:28.220
Th-Thank you…

00:19:32.680 --> 00:19:34.360
As for you…

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.300
Your room is always a mess, your feet smell,

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:38.980
and you snore so loud I can hear it in my room!

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:41.140
It's a goddamn nuisance!

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:54.340
Hey! You don't get to only talk smack about me!

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:58.920
Don't you have one nice thing
to say about your partner?!

00:19:59.400 --> 00:20:01.860
Hey, wake up! Come on, man!

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.740
You think this is funny?!

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:10.580
So, how's Shiratori's project proposal going?
Think it'll go well?

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:13.220
I'm sure it'll work out somehow.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:16.780
A-Are you okay?

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:18.580
Nope…

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:19.840
Want some water?

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:22.800
Never seen a newbie come
to work with a hangover!

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:25.520
Keep it up and you'll make it big in the industry!

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:27.500
My head… I'm gonna puke…

00:20:27.520 --> 00:20:28.900
You really think he'll be okay?

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:32.260
Yes, I'm… sure everything will work out!

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:33.820
Probably.

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:44.360
You've got a tournament ahead of you,
so polish up those skills!

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:46.380
Hit every damn shot, got it?

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:48.540
Give me all you've got!

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:49.400
Yes, sir!

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:51.980
Gather 'round.

00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:59.360
This is our bracket for this year's Tournament.

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:03.260
We're in with Tomari Transport,
one of the three powerhouses.

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:06.500
Once we beat Tomari,
we get to play against Unisics…

00:21:06.940 --> 00:21:10.500
And we gotta beat them to get our revenge.

00:21:10.600 --> 00:21:11.500
And we will.

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:13.880
Better do our best too.

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:15.220
As we always do!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:17.620
You know what that means…

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:19.660
Listen up!

00:21:19.660 --> 00:21:22.420
Give 'em hell from day one!

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:23.280
Yes, sir!

00:22:59.360 --> 00:23:02.000
The opening ceremony is about to begin.

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:05.280
All players, please line up with your teams.
